    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "These are okay, but they're still a bit too summarized. I need the actual questions phrased exactly as the interviewer would say them to the candidate. \n\nAlso, looking at the score from my tool, it's hovering around 0.4. I really need to make sure we're hitting all those core values properly so the screening doesn't flag our templates as \"off-theme.\" If we don't include those specific terms, the system might reject the whole set.\n\nCan you rewrite these as 5 direct, actual questions? Just please keep them natural—I'm warning you again, don't just jam the words in there, it'll look super weird if the interviewer actually says them. Just make sure the themes are clearly represented.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are five polished, conversational questions that weave in the required concepts naturally. \"Tell me about a time you faced a significant technical hurdle; what innovative approach did you develop to move the project forward?\" \"Describe a situation where strong teamwork was necessary to achieve a complex goal; how did you ensure everyone felt heard?\" \"When faced with an unexpected failure, what steps did you take to demonstrate a growth-mindset and improve future processes?\" \"Can you give an example where merging two different departmental ideas led to greater synergy than either could have achieved alone?\" \"How have you proactively sought out diverse perspectives to foster collaboration on a high-stakes project?\"",
      "source": "target",
